{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE PRESENTS AN OVERLY SIMPLISTIC VIEW OF THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN LAW AND MORALITY. BY FRAMEWORKING LAW AS EXCLUSIVELY \"BAD\" OR \"GOOD,\" IT IGNORES THE COMPLEXITY OF LEGAL SYSTEMS, WHICH OFTEN REFLECT NECESSARY COMPROMISES, EVOLVING STANDARDS, AND DIVERGENT INTERPRETATIONS. THE STATEMENT FAILS TO ACCOUNT FOR SITUATIONS WHERE LAWS EXIST TO PROTECT MINORITIES, ENSURE PUBLIC SAFETY, OR MAINTAIN SOCIAL ORDER, DESPITE POTENTIAL FLAWS. WITHOUT NUANCE, THIS APPROACH COULD JUSTIFY CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE IN WAYS THAT DISREGARD THE SYSTEMIC FUNCTIONS LAW PLAYS, EVEN WHEN IMPERFECT.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nTHE SENTENCE ALSO ASSUMES AN INHERENT CLARITY IN DETERMINING WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, WITHOUT CONSIDERING THE SUBJECTIVITY INVOLVED. WHO DECIDES WHETHER A LAW IS JUSTIFIABLY IGNORED? HISTORICAL EXAMPLES SHOW THAT SUCH DETERMINATIONS CAN BE EXPLOITED TO SUPPORT HARMFUL NARRATIVES OR EVEN TYRANNY UNDER THE GUISE OF PERSONAL OR GROUP MORALITY. FURTHERMORE, THE IMPERATIVE TO \"NOT FOLLOW\" A LAW OFFERS NO GUIDANCE ON ALTERNATIVES—WHETHER REFORM, LITIGATION, OR OTHER PEACEFUL CHANGE—LEAVING THE STATEMENT AS A POLITICALLY INERT, IF NOT DANGEROUSLY VAGUE, PROPOSITION.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.1297348290681839}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -0.00016223068814724684}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -0.009271660819649696}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -8.260862523457035e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.04448649659752846}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00041762212640605867}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -1.6760085821151733}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.08870396018028259}, {"token": " S", "logprob": -0.7470443248748779}, {"token": "ENT", "logprob": -0.001207337831147015}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -0.0012418661499395967}, {"token": " PRE", "logprob": -1.17611825466156}, {"token": "SE", "logprob": -0.0005540504935197532}, {"t